  "body": "Governing chain: UMR-20260806-171945-5767 -> UMR-20260808-074726-d105.\n\n`master_issue_tracker` (986 real rows: 981 migrated from `UMR_5767_ISSUE_RESOLUTION_MATRIX.json`, 5 real OCID-020 GTM-certification category failures) had a real, correct schema and real data, but the only way to write a new row was a one-off script run once from `/tmp` (`/tmp/build_master_issue_tracker.py`) — not a permanent, callable mechanism. Owner directive: make this tracker permanent and mandatory for any AI agent or deterministic script that finds a real issue.\n\n## What this adds (zero new files, extends the existing canonical `superboss-register.py`)\n\n- `_ensure_master_issue_tracker_table()` — idempotent `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`, byte-identical to the real live schema (confirmed via `PRAGMA table_info` before writing), wired into `_migrate_schema()`.\n- `add_master_issue()` / `close_master_issue()` / `update_master_issue()` / `query_master_issues()` + thin `cmd_*` CLI wrappers, following this file's own established conventions (no-commit functions, caller owns the transaction; mutable-column allowlist with `ValueError` on unknown/protected fields — see `update_gtm_certification_category()`'s precedent).\n- CLI: `add-issue`, `close-issue`, `update-issue`, `list-issues`. `list-issues` JSON output matches `--query-umr`'s own `{count, matches}` convention.\n\n## Real, independently-verified boolean tests\n\nRun against a throwaway `cp` of the real DB (`SUPERBOSS_REGISTER_DB` env override — this file's own documented test seam; production DB never touched):\n\n- `add-issue` → real new row, verified by direct `SELECT`.\n- duplicate `--issue-id` → real `ValueError`, exit 1.\n- missing both `--linked-ocid`/`--linked-umr-id` → real `ValueError`, exit 1.\n- `update-issue` with an invalid enum value → real `sqlite3.IntegrityError` (the table's own CHECK constraint), exit 1.\n- `update-issue` on a protected column (`created_at`) → real `ValueError`.\n- `close-issue` with blank `--resolution-notes` → real `ValueError`, exit 1.\n- `close-issue` with real notes → `issue_resolved_permanently=YES`, `is_closed=YES`, `apply_fix_notes` set — verified by direct `SELECT`.\n- `list-issues --is-closed`/`--linked-ocid` filters → real JSON.\n\nDiff is purely additive (354 insertions, 0 deletions) — branched from a fresh `origin/main` in an isolated worktree, not the shared live checkout, since the live checkout at `/opt/veridian/scripts` was ~97 commits behind `origin/main` with unrelated concurrent-session changes in the working tree.\n\nPart 2 of 3 of the same Owner directive (README-SERVER.md documentation + a real `resource_governor.py` gate hook) tracked separately in the task's own `PROGRESS.md`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
